- [ ] **Step 4: Implement the minimal deterministic scheduler/controller**

Use a phase lattice:

```cpp
std::uint32_t phaseIndex(std::uint32_t frame, std::uint32_t grid)
{
    grid = std::max(grid, 1u);
    return frame % (grid * grid);
}

bool scheduledPixel(std::uint32_t x, std::uint32_t y, std::uint32_t frame, std::uint32_t grid)
{
    grid = std::max(grid, 1u);
    const std::uint32_t phase = phaseIndex(frame, grid);
    return (x % grid) + (y % grid) * grid == phase;
}
```

Controller rules:
- initial grid = 2
- allowed grid range = 1..8
- quality floor maps to maximum allowed grid with `1 + round((1-quality) * 7)`
- exponential frame average: 90% previous, 10% new sample
- over budget threshold = `target_frame_ms * 1.10`; after 3 consecutive over-budget observations increment grid by one, capped by quality floor
- under budget threshold = `target_frame_ms * 1.02`; after 12 consecutive under-budget observations decrement grid by one, floored at 1
- samples <= 0 or > 250 ms are ignored so startup/debugger stalls do not destroy state

